       The mmqq__ooppeenn() library function is implemented on top of a system call
       of the same name.  The library function performs the check that the
       _n_a_m_e starts with a slash (/), giving the EEIINNVVAALL error if it does not.
       The kernel system call expects _n_a_m_e to contain no preceding slash, so
       the C library function passes _n_a_m_e without the preceding slash (i.e.,
       _n_a_m_e_+_1) to the system call.

